Subject: Features available in Bio7 (Eclipse RCP)
Message-ID: <52606278.2090908@mbacou.com>

Hi Stephan,

I just recently started using Bio7 http://bio7.org/ developed by Marcel 
Austenfeld. I don't do any ecological modeling, but as a heavy R (and 
StatET) user, I am really impressed with some of Bio7 R-specific 
features like:
- in-cell table editing
- quick copy/paste/import/export of vectors, matrices, and 
dataframes/datatables
- quick import and visualization of raster/vector layers and integration 
with ImageJ
- flowchart model editor for complex tasks

I think it'd be fantastic if some of these features were available in 
StatET or in a separate Eclipse plug-in.

Also with regards to remoting to external R servers, how does RJ server 
compare to using Rserve inside Eclipse?

Thanks to you both, --Mel.

